s`, `github_get_pr_comments`, `github_create_comment`, `github_resolve_pr_thread`, `github_reply_to_pr_thread`, `github_search_issues`, `github_create_issue` — restoring the documented parity contract for future suites too.\n2. **Or mock the keys in this test's globals bag** (the repo convention — \"mock all dmtools globals\"): `mMergeGate({ github_add_labels: fn, github_get_pr_review_threads: fn, github_get_pr_comments: fn, github_create_comment: fn, github_resolve_pr_thread: fn })`. The sibling test (`github_add_labels: undefined` → `null`) already covers the capability-miss mapping, so no coverage is lost.\n\nVerify with the command CI runs: `node js/unit-tests/node_testRunner.js $(node -e \"console.log(require('./js/unit-tests/run_all.json').params.jobParams.testFiles.join(' '))\")` → expect `PASS — 9390 passed, 0 failed`."
